# Rank 1783 / CVE-2014-3527 (SEC-2688, CWE-346 origin validation, recorded
# CWE-20/918 by the nearest shipped concepts):
# spring-projects/spring-security's CAS proxy-ticket authentication takes the
# service URL -- the audience the CAS server matches a presented ticket
# against -- from `ServiceAuthenticationDetails.getServiceUrl()`.
# DefaultServiceAuthenticationDetails
# (cas/src/main/java/org/springframework/security/cas/web/authentication/
# DefaultServiceAuthenticationDetails.java:53 at the parent) assembles it as
#
#   this.serviceUrl = UrlUtils.buildFullRequestUrl(request.getScheme(),
#           request.getServerName(), request.getServerPort(),
#           request.getRequestURI(), query);
#
# with `query` the request's query string minus the artifact (ticket)
# parameter. The servlet container resolves all three authority accessors from
# the client's own Host header, so the client picks the audience a proxy ticket
# is validated for: a ticket minted for a service the attacker controls
# validates as genuine. The fixed revision's own regression test names the property
# (`getServiceUrlDoesNotUseHostHeader`, `request.setServerName("evil.com")`
# must still yield `https://example.com/...`).
#
# 934937d9c1dc20c396b96c08310b72cfa627acbf fixes it by parsing the configured
# service (`new URL(casService)`) and taking protocol, host and port from that
# URL instead, while `request.getRequestURI()` and the cleaned query still come
# from the request -- the path legitimately mirrors the request, the authority
# must not. ServiceProperties.afterPropertiesSet() also drops the
# `authenticateAllArtifacts` exemption so a configured `service` is mandatory,
# and ServiceAuthenticationDetailsSource grows a ServiceProperties constructor
# plus an ApplicationContextAware fallback. The remediation is present at the
# commit and absent at its parent f50e058d0, so both halves of the 1390 check
# hold and the pool row is correct in every field; no correction needed.
#
# What fires today. `timeout 180 ./bin/vyql scan --cache off --max-ram 6GB`
# over spring-security/cas, three runs per side, is 3 findings and 20 flags on
# both revisions -- byte-identical rows, all three findings being VYQL-INJ-009
# log formatting in CasAuthenticationFilter, all twenty flags being
# core.AuthenticationCheck in the test sources. `scan -flags only` puts no flag
# or finding in DefaultServiceAuthenticationDetails.java or
# ServiceAuthenticationDetailsSource.java on either side. `vyql match` on the
# class labels `request.getRequestURI()` and `request.getQueryString()` as
# code.HttpInput and leaves getScheme/getServerName/getServerPort unlabelled;
# UrlUtils.buildFullRequestUrl is unbound.
#
# The blocker splits into a breadth half and a visibility half.
#
# Breadth: reading the request's scheme, host and port is the servlet API's
# documented request-mirroring idiom, not a defect by itself. Measured with a
# function-scoped probe over the real code, the three accessors together fire
# on 5 functions in spring-security -- the vulnerable constructor plus
# UrlUtils.buildFullRequestUrl(HttpServletRequest) (whose javadoc is "the full
# URL the client make the request"), DefaultSavedRequest's constructor
# and doesRequestMatch, and LoginUrlAuthenticationEntryPoint's
# buildRedirectUrlToLoginPage -- and on roughly 52 functions across 19 Java
# trees under /tmp/cve-work/rank*/ (9 in spring-framework alone: CorsUtils,
# ServletUriComponentsBuilder, WebUtils, ForwardedHeaderFilter tests, servlet
# mocks). Every one of those is a correct mirror.
#
# Visibility: the property that makes this a vulnerability -- that the URL is
# the audience a credential validates against -- is stated nowhere in the
# vulnerable function. It is consumed two files away in
# CasAuthenticationProvider.getServiceUrl(authentication), through
# `((ServiceAuthenticationDetails)authentication.getDetails()).getServiceUrl()`,
# an interface-typed receiver the engine never routes into the concrete
# override (the gap filed at rank 1339, which is why Log4Shell is likewise
# undetected on real code), and the path then runs through a constructor field
# write and a getter besides. That consumer is identical in both revisions, so
# it cannot discriminate either.
#
# Alternatives measured and rejected:
#  - narrowing to the three accessors plus a URL-assembly call: 7 functions
#    across 4 trees, 1 true positive (CorsUtils.isCorsRequest and
#    ShiroHttpServletResponse.doIsEncodeable are origin checks, not defects);
#  - narrowing to the three accessors plus a java.util.regex.Pattern-typed
#    parameter (the ticket-excision pattern): exactly the vulnerable
#    constructor in spring-security and nothing in spring-framework, shiro or
#    openam -- but the parameter's type is a rarity filter with no documented
#    connection to the weakness, and the three-accessor conjunction is itself
#    this implementation's spelling of "the request's absolute URL": the
#    idiomatic request.getRequestURL() form, and any non-regex excision, walk
#    past it;
#  - class scope with the excision call: 1 true positive plus 2 hits on
#    openam's 2700-line SAML2Utils and AuthClientUtils, where a replaceAll at
#    line 1355 satisfies a clause about the request reads at line 2297 -- the
#    co-membership failure mode;
#  - keying on ServiceAuthenticationDetails itself: it has exactly one
#    implementation in the ecosystem scanned, so the binding's only possible
#    instance is this fix.
# The 1380 counterweight does not apply: the fixed revision does leave API-documented
# calls inside the method it guards (the three servlet authority accessors),
# but keying on them is the 52-site mirror detector above.
#
# The four cases: (a) and (b) are the two real revisions and record the miss;
# (c) is the request-mirror idiom the flaw half cannot be separated from, and
# must stay a reject on both halves -- a rule that fired on it would flag
# correct code throughout any servlet application. Flipping (a) to expect
# needs a fact that ties a reconstructed URL to the credential validation that
# consumes it, which is cross-file through an interface today.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-vocabulary-gap, all three cases rejected.
# (b) and (c) are correct code and must remain rejects.

test "rank1783: (a) the CAS service URL -- the audience a proxy ticket validates against -- is assembled from the request's own scheme, host and port"
  lang java
  file cas/src/main/java/org/springframework/security/cas/web/authentication/DefaultServiceAuthenticationDetails.java
  reject VYQL-RF-010
  reject VYQL-AUTH-003
  reject VYQL-RF-045
  code
  ```
  package org.springframework.security.cas.web.authentication;

  import java.util.regex.Pattern;
  import javax.servlet.http.HttpServletRequest;
  import org.springframework.security.web.util.UrlUtils;

  final class DefaultServiceAuthenticationDetails implements ServiceAuthenticationDetails {
    private final String serviceUrl;

    DefaultServiceAuthenticationDetails(HttpServletRequest request, Pattern artifactPattern) {
      final String query = getQueryString(request, artifactPattern);
      this.serviceUrl = UrlUtils.buildFullRequestUrl(request.getScheme(),
              request.getServerName(), request.getServerPort(),
              request.getRequestURI(), query);
    }

    public String getServiceUrl() {
      return serviceUrl;
    }

    private String getQueryString(final HttpServletRequest request, final Pattern artifactPattern) {
      final String query = request.getQueryString();
      if (query == null) {
        return null;
      }
      final String result = artifactPattern.matcher(query).replaceFirst("");
      if (result.length() == 0) {
        return null;
      }
      return result.startsWith("&") ? result.substring(1) : result;
    }
  }
  ```

test "rank1783: (b) the fixed revision takes protocol, host and port from the configured service URL, keeping only the request's path and cleaned query"
  lang java
  file cas/src/main/java/org/springframework/security/cas/web/authentication/DefaultServiceAuthenticationDetails.java
  reject VYQL-RF-010
  reject VYQL-AUTH-003
  reject VYQL-RF-045
  code
  ```
  package org.springframework.security.cas.web.authentication;

  import java.net.MalformedURLException;
  import java.net.URL;
  import java.util.regex.Pattern;
  import javax.servlet.http.HttpServletRequest;
  import org.springframework.security.web.util.UrlUtils;

  final class DefaultServiceAuthenticationDetails implements ServiceAuthenticationDetails {
    private final String serviceUrl;

    DefaultServiceAuthenticationDetails(String casService, HttpServletRequest request, Pattern artifactPattern)
        throws MalformedURLException {
      URL casServiceUrl = new URL(casService);
      int port = getServicePort(casServiceUrl);
      final String query = getQueryString(request, artifactPattern);
      this.serviceUrl = UrlUtils.buildFullRequestUrl(casServiceUrl.getProtocol(),
              casServiceUrl.getHost(), port,
              request.getRequestURI(), query);
    }

    public String getServiceUrl() {
      return serviceUrl;
    }

    private static int getServicePort(URL casServiceUrl) {
      int port = casServiceUrl.getPort();
      if (port == -1) {
        port = casServiceUrl.getDefaultPort();
      }
      return port;
    }

    private String getQueryString(final HttpServletRequest request, final Pattern artifactPattern) {
      final String query = request.getQueryString();
      if (query == null) {
        return null;
      }
      final String result = artifactPattern.matcher(query).replaceFirst("");
      if (result.length() == 0) {
        return null;
      }
      return result.startsWith("&") ? result.substring(1) : result;
    }
  }
  ```

test "rank1783: (c) the same three accessors in their documented role -- mirroring the request the client actually made -- which a rule on the accessors alone cannot be separated from"
  lang java
  file cas/src/main/java/org/springframework/security/cas/web/authentication/UrlUtils.java
  reject VYQL-RF-010
  reject VYQL-AUTH-003
  reject VYQL-RF-045
  code
  ```
  package org.springframework.security.cas.web.authentication;

  import javax.servlet.http.HttpServletRequest;

  public final class UrlUtils {
    public static String buildFullRequestUrl(HttpServletRequest r) {
      return buildFullRequestUrl(r.getScheme(), r.getServerName(), r.getServerPort(), r.getRequestURI(),
              r.getQueryString());
    }

    public static String buildFullRequestUrl(String scheme, String serverName, int serverPort, String requestURI,
            String queryString) {
      scheme = scheme.toLowerCase();
      boolean includePort = true;
      if (serverPort == (scheme.equals("http") ? 80 : 443)) {
        includePort = false;
      }
      return scheme + "://" + serverName + (includePort ? ":" + serverPort : "") + requestURI
              + (queryString == null ? "" : "?" + queryString);
    }
  }
  ```
